  "worked_solution": "The function $f(x)$ is the sum of three power functions. So, we apply the sum rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =3{x}^{(3-1)}+(-2){x}^{(-2-1)}-1 \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-2{x}^{-3}-1 \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
